\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The slow drift is quadratic}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{On the #{x}-axis the system
##{\dot x=x^{2},\qquad \dot y=-y}
of \citet{(3.2.1), §3.2, p. 124}{guckenheimer1983nonlinear} has
velocity #{\dot x=x^{2}}. For #{x<0} that velocity points toward
the origin.}

\p{\citet{Remark (2), §5.1.1, pp. 159–160}{kuznetsov2004elements}
records a family of [center manifolds](fnip-0059) for a planar
equilibrium with eigenvalues #{0} and #{-1}: the graphs
#{y=\beta e^{1/x}} for #{x<0}, joined to #{y=0} for #{x\ge 0}.
\citet{Theorem 5.2, §5.1.1, p. 161}{kuznetsov2004elements} is the
reduction principle. Near the equilibrium the flow is locally
topologically equivalent to the motion on one
[center manifold](fnip-0059) together with the linear flow on a
complementary space, and the reduced equations coming from two
[center manifolds](fnip-0059) are locally
smoothly equivalent.}
